[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Bulwark Lite can be served by a web server of your own (A) or run as an
application inside Stalwart (B).

A) Web server

1. Set jmapServerUrl in %%WWWDIR%%/config.json to your
   JMAP server, e.g. https://mail.example.com.

2. Serve %%WWWDIR%% at the root of a (virtual) host. Deep links
   need a rewrite to the shell of each section; with the EXAMPLES option
   there are configurations for nginx and Caddy in
   %%EXAMPLESDIR%%.

3. Allow the browser to talk to the JMAP server (CORS). In Stalwart,
   enable "Permissive CORS policy" under Settings > Network > HTTP >
   Security.

B) Stalwart application

The Stalwart bundle is built into %%BUNDLE%%
from the upstream bundle and the files in %%ETCDIR%%/stalwart:
each file there (except *.sample) replaces or adds the file of the same
path in the bundle. This happens on every install and upgrade of this
package; after a change of your own, run

  %%PREFIX%%/sbin/bulwark-lite-stalwart

1. Optional: edit %%ETCDIR%%/stalwart/config.json, e.g. to set
   loginCompanyName, loginImprintUrl or loginPrivacyPolicyUrl, then run
   bulwark-lite-stalwart as above. Leave jmapServerUrl empty: the app
   then talks to the Stalwart server that serves it, and needs no CORS.

2. Let Stalwart load the bundle from the local file and mount it at
   /webmail (Stalwart 1.0 or later; the user "stalwart" must be able to
   read the file):

     stalwart-cli create Application \
       --field description='Bulwark Webmail' \
       --field resourceUrl='file://%%BUNDLE%%' \
       --field 'urlPrefix={"/webmail":true}'
     stalwart-cli create Action/UpdateApps

   or, in the web admin, add the same under Settings > Web Applications
   and run Actions > Update applications.

   Without changes of your own, the unmodified upstream bundle works
   as well, either the copy in this package or the latest release
   straight from upstream, which needs no package at all:

     resourceUrl='file://%%DATADIR%%/bulwark-lite-stalwart.zip'
     resourceUrl='https://github.com/bulwarkmail/webmail/releases/latest/download/bulwark-lite-stalwart.zip'

3. Stalwart only reads the bundle when its applications are updated:
   after every upgrade of this package or rebuild of the bundle, run
   "stalwart-cli create Action/UpdateApps" (or "Update applications")
   again. This reloads all applications, so check that every
   resourceUrl is reachable first.

See %%DOCSDIR%%/LITE-README.md (DOCS option) for details.
EOM
}
]
